{
    "$comment": [
        "Embed providers are deployment configuration, not catalogue data.",
        "TMDB has no opinion about third-party embed hosts, so this file is the source of truth.",
        "Placeholders: {{tmdb}} {{imdb}} {{slug}} {{kind}} {{season}} {{episode}}",
        "A provider whose placeholder cannot be filled for a given title is skipped at",
        "request time and reported in the `rejected` array of the servers response.",
        "Any host in `hosts` must also be present in src/config/constants.ts ALLOWED_EMBED_HOSTS.",
        "Redirect chains are resolved server-side by src/services/embedGuard.service.ts before a",
        "URL reaches the browser. A chain that enters BLOCKED_AD_HOSTS or leaves the allowlist",
        "rejects the provider; the iframe only ever receives the final URL.",
        "This replaces the former iframe `sandbox`: a 302 is resolved by the network stack before",
        "any attribute is read, so `sandbox` never prevented one. Note that no host here can have",
        "its in-frame ads stripped - that is same-origin policy. Keep this list to hosts that are",
        "authorized to be embedded.",
        "`kinds` restricts a row to movies or TV: a TV-only template embeds {{season}}/{{episode}}",
        "which cannot resolve for movies."
    ],
